  greetings:
  - Shh. They're resting.
  - Oh, a visitor. Come into the light. Everything does.
  aboutSelf: I collect moths. Two thousand, four hundred and six. They come to the light. Everything does, eventually.
  aboutTown: Semblance was here before the highway. Before the maps. It will be here after.
  seenAnythingStrange: The moths stopped coming to my porch light last week. Something else is drawing them.
  foundersDay: Rain. Lovely rain. The moths hate it. Mae's cherry pie, of course.
  gossip:
  - title: About Silas Thorne
    response: Silas wears his wedding ring on his right hand. The Thornes always have. Odd family.
  - title: About June Marsh
    response: June's eyes are set so wide. Like a deer's. A prey animal.
